From ff64370e003f6144167c4f907fc904d3fc4a3b4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build-engine <build-engine@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:54:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(drama3): reuse a voice reference's prefill across
 requests

Metal kept no prefix state: every speech request reset the engine and
re-ran the whole prompt, so a cloned voice paid its reference prefill
again on each call (measured 3.3 s of a 4.7 s first-audio time here).

The request now carries the number of leading rows that are the voice
reference. The Metal host prefills that prefix once per lane, snapshots
the recurrent state and counters, and on a later request with the same
prefix restores the snapshot and prefills only the per-request rows.
The snapshot is keyed by the reference rows themselves, so a different
voice rebuilds it. CUDA keeps the old path.

Audio is unchanged: replies are byte-identical to the uncached engine
for the same prompt and seed.
---
 zig/src/core/speech_api.zig              |  2 +
 zig/src/families/drama3/drama3_metal.zig |  1 +
 zig/src/families/drama3/metal/engine.zig | 72 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 zig/src/native/drama_host.zig            | 61 +++++++++++++++++---
 zig/src/server/speech.zig                |  8 +++
 5 files changed, 135 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/zig/src/core/speech_api.zig b/zig/src/core/speech_api.zig
